Here is the corresponding csharp code that uses "Debug.Assert":

```cs
void LoadTemplates(string fileName)
{
	bool templatesFileExist = File.Exists(fileName);
	// @@@ the template file exists
	Debug.Assert(templatesFileExist, "The template file does not exist.");
}
```

The Debug.Assert statement checks if the "templatesFileExist" condition is true. If it's not true, it will throw an AssertionFailedException with the message "The template file does not exist.".
